\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 There are two philosophies.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Option A \'97 Node-centric\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Each GX10 manages its own models.\
Core asks:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "Can you run Llama 4?"\strokec2 \
Node replies:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "Sure."\
This is how a lot of existing inference systems work.\
I 
\f1\b don't
\f0\b0  like it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Option B \'97 Core-centric (my recommendation)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 HAL Core owns a 
\f1\b Model Registry
\f0\b0 .\
Imagine it like an air traffic controller.\
