\cf0 \strokec2 A 
\f1\b very active lifetime archive
\f0\b0  could contain hundreds of millions of tokens and still occupy only a few gigabytes for the original text. Even with redundant indexes, embeddings, summaries, provenance records, and backups, it would probably remain in the 
\f1\b tens of gigabytes
\f0\b0 , not terabytes.\
For perspective, suppose you averaged:\
