\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 The architectural conclusion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Storage capacity is not a meaningful reason to discard routine conversations.
\f0\b0 \
The real reasons to distinguish archive from memory are:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Retrieval quality:
\f0\b0  HAL should not inject every old conversation into current requests.\
\ls17\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Privacy and retention:
\f0\b0  some interactions may deserve expiration or explicit deletion.\
\ls17\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Memory accuracy:
\f0\b0  casual statements should not automatically become enduring facts.\
\ls17\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Computational cost:
\f0\b0  continuously re-indexing and reinterpreting everything has a cost, although still manageable locally.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 So I would support the revised approach:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Archive every conversation by default, but selectively promote information into active memory.
\f0\b0 \
HAL\'92s conversation archive can remain complete and searchable. Its Memory Graph contains distilled, current knowledge. Its episodic layer records meaningful events and decisions. The archive preserves provenance and allows future, better models to reinterpret the original exchanges.\
On a 
\f1\b 20 TB NAS
\f0\b0 , even an exceptionally detailed lifetime text history would be a rounding error. The question is not whether HAL can afford to retain it\'97it plainly can. The question is how intelligently and transparently HAL uses it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
